            </connector>
            <label>All Kill Switches Clear</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Checked per-Benefit since Get Records can&#39;t filter Benefit by a cross-object Program field, and Decision conditions don&#39;t support In against a collection. colActiveProgramIdsText is a semicolon-delimited string of active Program Ids (e.g. &quot;id1;id2;id3;&quot;); since Ids never contain &quot;;&quot; and are fixed-length, a Contains match can only align with a full stored Id, never a cross-entry substring. Benefits under inactive Programs are skipped and left untouched.</description>
        <name>Is_Program_Active</name>
        <label>Is Program Active?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Loop_Related_Benefits</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Program Not Active</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Program_Is_Active</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>colActiveProgramIdsText</leftValueReference>
                <operator>Contains</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>Loop_Related_Benefits.ProgramId</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Build_Updated_Benefit_Record</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Program Is Active</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>DWDECI-119. Admin screen flow: edits an existing Service Type (BenefitType - Name, Unit of Measure, Active) and cascades the new Name, Unit of Measure, and Active/IsActive value to every child Benefit record tied to this Service Type across all currently-active Programs, in a single bulk Update Records call (governor-limit safe for 200+ child records). Deactivation is soft (Active__c/IsActive = false) - past Benefit Assignments and associations remain intact and reportable, per ticket decision. Benefits under inactive Programs are left untouched. Get Records filters/queriedFields cannot reliably use a cross-object relationship path (e.g. Program.IsActive, Program.Name off Benefit) - confirmed via deploy: a single such path silently corrupts to a bogus field reference instead of failing, and two together hard-fail the deploy with a duplicate-value error - so this flow avoids relationship paths entirely: active Programs are queried directly and their Ids concatenated into colActiveProgramIdsText (a delimited string, since Decision conditions don&#39;t support In against a collection either) and membership is checked per-Benefit with a Contains condition on that string, and the new Benefit Name is built with SUBSTITUTE() against the Benefit&#39;s own current Name rather than reading Program.Name. Fault paths -&gt; ErrorLogger.logFromFlow (ACC Base Utilities Log Error action). Gated by the global master kill switch and its own named-automation kill switch.</description>
    <dynamicChoiceSets>
        <name>AllServiceTypeChoices</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <displayField>Name</displayField>
        <object>BenefitType</object>
        <sortField>Name</sortField>
        <sortOrder>Asc</sortOrder>
        <valueField>Id</valueField>
    </dynamicChoiceSets>
    <dynamicChoiceSets>
        <name>UnitOfMeasureChoices</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <displayField>Name</displayField>
        <object>UnitOfMeasure</object>
        <sortField>Name</sortField>
        <sortOrder>Asc</sortOrder>
        <valueField>Id</valueField>
    </dynamicChoiceSets>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Rebuilds the Benefit&#39;s Name by replacing the old Service Type name with the new one, preserving whatever suffix (e.g. the Program name) is already there. Avoids needing to read Program.Name off Benefit, which Get Records can&#39;t do reliably here.</description>
        <name>UpdatedBenefitNameFormula</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>SUBSTITUTE({!Loop_Related_Benefits.Name}, {!Get_Service_Type.Name}, {!ServiceTypeName})</expression>
    </formulas>
